; Windows-pnpm workspace-discovery isolation.
;
; Why this file exists:
;   pnpm walks UP from the project to find a `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. On the
;   Windows dev box used during Phase A.2 + A.3, a stray
;   `C:\Users\Steve\pnpm-workspace.yaml` (from an unrelated project) sat
;   above this repo on the path. pnpm picked it up silently and rewrote
;   `node_modules` to land in the home directory instead of `pwa/`, which
;   broke local `pnpm build` until the workspace flag was explicitly passed.
;
;   `ignore-workspace=true` pins pnpm to treat this directory as a stand-
;   alone package no matter what `pnpm-workspace.yaml` it finds upstream.
;   The repo is single-package (only `pwa/` ships) so there's no real
;   workspace to lose — and CI never tripped on this because the GitHub
;   runner doesn't carry the stray file in $HOME.
;
; Reference: see Phase A.3 PR #6 commit messages for the original
; reproduction.

ignore-workspace=true
